
# Commands Used – Network Reconnaissance

## 1. Network Information Gathering

### Display IP Address
```bash
hostname -I
```
Displays the IP address assigned to the system.

### Display Network Interfaces
```bash
ip addr
```
Displays available network interfaces and their IP configurations.

### Display Routing Table
```bash
ip route
```
Displays the system's routing information.

### Check Network Connectivity
```bash
ping -c 4 <gateway>
```
Checks connectivity with the specified gateway.

### View DNS Configuration
```bash
cat /etc/resolv.conf
```
Displays configured DNS resolver information.

### DNS Lookup
```bash
nslookup example.com
```
Queries DNS records for a domain.

## 2. Web Directory Enumeration

```bash
gobuster dir -u http://<LAB-IP>/ -w /usr/share/wordlists/dirb/common.txt
```

Used to discover directories and files on an authorized lab web server.

## 3. Subdomain Enumeration

```bash
subfinder -d example.com -o subdomains.txt
```

Used to identify subdomains of the selected domain.

## 4. Remove Duplicate Subdomains

```bash
sort -u subdomains.txt -o subdomains_unique.txt
```

Removes duplicate entries from the collected subdomain list.

## 5. DNS Resolution

```bash
dnsx -l subdomains_unique.txt -o resolved.txt
```

Checks which discovered subdomains resolve through DNS.

## Disclaimer

All reconnaissance activities should be performed only on systems and domains for which permission has been granted. Replace example.com and <LAB-IP> with the actual authorized lab target where applicable.
